# DB state after the fleet's hour: table port_hosts, 127 rows.
#
# Written by: PortStatsCollector.collectDeviceHosts (Tier 3b) → queries.UpsertPortHosts
# The hour:   the call-plan fleet of 5 fake devices (callplan_harness_test.go), every scheduled loop,
#             one simulated hour and a minute from 2026-01-05 12:00 UTC; the devices' counters, CPU,
#             memory and uptime move with the clock (callplan_motion_test.go)
#
# A change in this file is a change in what the pollers store.
# Rewrite it with: go test ./internal/poller -run TestDBState -update
#
# Normalised (dbstate_test.go):
#   first_seen: the simulated clock, as the offset from the start of the hour; stored as TEXT "2006-01-02 15:04:05" (as CURRENT_TIMESTAMP writes it)
#   last_seen: the simulated clock, as the offset from the start of the hour; stored as TEXT "2006-01-02 15:04:05" (as CURRENT_TIMESTAMP writes it)
#   REAL values with three decimals, strings quoted, NULL as NULL
#   rows ordered by the primary key (device_id, interface_name, mac_address)

